# FreightProof Receiver — required environment variables
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the value.

# FastAPI backend base URL (no trailing slash).
#
# MUST be an address the RECEIVER'S OWN PHONE can reach, not this machine's loopback.
# The receiver opens this app from a QR code on their own device, so `localhost` here
# resolves to the phone, the very first request fails at the network layer, and the page
# reports "This link is no longer valid" — the client cannot tell a dead token from a
# dead connection, by design (see HandoverPageClient's anti-oracle comment).
#
# Local development over a phone: this machine's LAN address, e.g. http://192.168.1.5:8000
# (`ipconfig getifaddr en0`). It changes when the network does — if handovers start
# failing instantly after a network switch, this value is the first thing to check.
#
# Keep it in step with the backend's HANDOVER_RECEIVER_BASE_URL: that is what the QR
# points at AND what the API folds into its CORS allow-list (core/config.py,
# cors_allowed_origins). If one names an IP and the other names localhost, the handover
# fails with no visible cause.
#
# Deployed (Vercel, receiver.freightproof.co.za):
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.freightproof.co.za
# The subdomain is not cosmetic — the binding cookie is SameSite=Strict, so this app and
# the API must share a registrable domain. A *.vercel.app URL silently fails the binding
# check. See docs/deployment-runbook.md §1.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=
